{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact S4 repair head 78583ca77e45ddee0939dc50d52e5157cb7c1741 on builder/s4-enrol-role-fixture-20261112, all 55 artifacts, for request 9a053402 under promise abbd5eba and review request 561870b0. Repair manifest SHA-256 2e3b57a9930d19f69b85be388018fd07f8ddccea010d1f6def3cbb37efc486d4. The head meets both required changes of 6fbde9b8 and the scope of ruling 3ae8a396.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- Required change 1. `OAuthClients.admitControl` (`oauth-clients.ts:108-115`) now charges `address:` plus `addressKey(cf-connecting-ip)` before `key:` plus the actor, in the same purpose. An address refusal returns before the key window, so it allocates no key row. `mcpRoute` reads `cf-connecting-ip` once and passes it through `McpRegistry.admitControl` as the fifth argument (`worker-mcp.ts:57`, `119`, `206`). One address can therefore open at most 120 key rows for each purpose in one window. A missing address shares one `addressless` row. Cloudflare always sets the header, so that bucket matters only off the edge.\n- The witness in `hosted.scope.test.ts` drives 4,216 distinct actors per purpose through the real `OAuthClients` from one address. It then makes a fresh member's signed `create` from another address answer 201 and `retire` answer 202. It asserts 120 admitted, 120 key rows, no overflow row, and that the member's key never entered either window. Against 6352d355 the pair was [429, 429], and the Worker test saw the address argument as `undefined` (END 38477983). The test distinguishes.\n- Required change 2. `docs/hosted-mcp.md` no longer calls itself a checkpoint. It states the 4 KiB stored-row charge, the 15 MiB budget, the 1 MiB retire reserve, the `507` result and S10 af11896e, as 3ae8a396 item 3 asks. A new paragraph states the address-before-key order.\n- `credential` and `diff` now declare `_meta.ui.visibility: [\"model\"]` through a new optional `meta` argument, and `docs/mcp-tools.json` and the `view-resources.test.ts` expectation name both. The credential red at 6352d355 fails at that expectation (END a98bb878). The diff red stays masked behind it, as the note says.\n- The seal changes in `security-entry-points.test.mjs` cover exactly the four changed owners: `worker-mcp.ts` `mcpRoute` and `McpRegistry`, `McpService`, `oauth-clients.ts` and `oauth-routes.ts`.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 221e11c3 is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The builder's worktree is clean. Against main, the head changes exactly the 55 paths that the 55 artifacts cover, all at the head, none stale or retired. Since 6352d355 the head changes 12 paths.\n- Cheap checks. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The commit-message check passes: 35 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean.\n- The failed gate and its follow-up, under `docs/evidence-filing.md`. The gate at e708f454 exited 1 with one Native failure, the H6 scene in `hosted.scope.test.ts`. Every stage ran. e4051271 changes only that file, which nothing imports. The change reads the held reply inside the action and waits for it before cleanup. The hold, the role change, the assertions and the deadlines stay. The compiler and the whole 24-test Hosted owner passed under END 62722920. I accept the follow-up as evidence for source e4051271. The failed gate stays a failure, and the note claims no pass.\n- Retained controls under ruling 0528fc25. The note says the aggregate-budget case is one of the eight reds. Its deciding assertion runs before the changed `keyCalls` lines, and the source before them is unchanged from 6352d355. The manifest indexes that proof.\n- Evidence. All 114 files in the repair manifest match their SHA-256 values in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence`. The correspondence receipt hashes to `911aa98b…6c9e`, as the request says.\n- CI, under rulings 3a5c4448 and a8d2f83d. Card run 43293238065 is a push event, attempt 1, completed and successful, at 7841c856. From 7841c856 to the head only the note and the repair manifest change. Page run 43274401664 at 77ac8113 stands, because no path in the Page filter changed.\n- I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Admission stays in the one registry object, and the address comes from the edge header only at the Worker. Address and key windows share one table and one transaction, so a refused address leaves no row.\n\nSecurity: no finding against 6fbde9b8. One limit remains, and the note states it at line 62. The reference docs give no number. Each address and its 120 key rows take 121 of the 4,096 rows in a purpose. About 34 IPv4 addresses or IPv6 /64s, at about 4,100 calls a minute, therefore fill the control table, and 34 more fill cleanup. After that, a member whose address has no live row shares the 120-call overflow and can get 429 on `create` and `retire` in every room. One IPv6 /48 holds 65,536 /64s. S1 left the same kind of limit for creation. Before hosted MCP opens to rooms with unknown members, S10 or a later head should either count key rows only after the standing check or bound new key rows per address far lower, and state the number in `docs/hosted-mcp.md`.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The notes of 6fbde9b8 stand and belong to S10 under 3ae8a396. One more: the address and key charges repeat the same refusal mapping, and one local helper would hold it.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing, deployment or MCP enablement. The planner decides the landing and deploys afterward.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1441e32a7998f4763e896d77e52340f021af54ed","binding":"assigned","head":"78583ca77e45ddee0939dc50d52e5157cb7c1741","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5133190fdbf21b90a56008aed4410a91d1a7844f\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bf59d56f1d048a997bc0d418379cd330c1aeb72f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:abbd5eba6806777f902556d91b09d0566e107175\"